soc: sunxi: h713-mips: a standby that does not finish ends in the power gate

U-Boot writes "RUN1" into RTC GP5 at every boot and boots straight
through a reset that finds it; BL31 writes "GATE" there for a power-off,
and any word but "RUN1" sends U-Boot into its power gate, dark, waiting
for the key. A standby that does not finish ends in a reset - crust's
15 s budget when the board hangs going to sleep (C1), crust's budget or
the watchdog when Linux does not come back, the watchdog when the core
stalls the bus at its start - and with "RUN1" in place that reset boots
the board with the lamp on, in the middle of the night. The owner wants
it dark instead.

The driver now holds GP5 as a fourth reg (0x07090114, not requested,
the RTC driver holds the block). A PM notifier turns "RUN1" into "STBY"
at PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE, before the noirq window where C1 hangs. The mark
goes back to "RUN1" when the core runs again after its start out of the
park, or at PM_POST_SUSPEND when this sleep parked nothing, and before a
reboot that was asked for (reboot notifier, no lock), so that one still
boots. The word decides, not a flag: only "RUN1" becomes "STBY" and only
"STBY" goes back. U-Boot reads "STBY" as an unknown word: gate.

Not caught: crust itself hanging asleep, which only R_WDOG would reset.

Measured on the HY310 (r2test4 with this module and DTB, h713_gate=1,
09.10.2026): a standby through h713-power marks STBY and is back to RUN1
after the core's ready, picture back after 5.3 s; a test module hanging
syscore suspend: crust reset after 15000 ms, U-Boot "gate: cold start
(GP5 53544259)", dark until the power key; hanging syscore resume: crust
reset after 60000 ms, the same; a reboot with STBY in place (core left
parked) boots through, "warm start (GP5 52554e31)". W=1 without
warnings.

